  "title": "Savitribai Phule",
  "summary": "Savitribai Phule and her husband Jyotiba Phule started a girls' school at Bhidewada in Budhwar Peth, Pune, in 1848, with her as its first teacher. By 1851 they ran three schools in the Pune area. She faced opposition and is remembered as a pioneer of girls' education in India.",
